---
import AgentPage from '../../components/home/AgentPage.astro';
---
<AgentPage
  name={"Pi"}
  logo={"/assets/agents/pi.svg"}
  headline={"Run Pi in parallel."}
  sub={"A worktree and terminal per task, status from a Pi extension Ouijit installs, and the ouijit command in its system prompt. Nothing to configure."}
  description={"Run Pi in parallel with Ouijit: a git worktree and terminal per task, live status through a Pi extension, and the ouijit CLI in its system prompt."}
  points={[
    ["Knows Ouijit", "The ouijit CLI reference is appended to the system prompt at launch, so Pi can create tasks, move cards and stage review comments without being told how."],
    ["Live status", "Pi exposes its lifecycle to extensions, so Ouijit installs a small one and loads it at launch. It reports when a turn starts and ends, and the card shows thinking or ready."],
    ["Sandboxed", "Run it with its permission prompts off inside Ouijit's sandbox and the kernel holds it to the task's worktree. The dev server beside it stays on the host."],
  ]}
  hooks={"<span class=\"dim\"># Start · a task moves to In Progress</span>\npi"}
  faqs={[
    ["Can it sign in inside the sandbox?", "Yes. The sandbox profile includes nono's Pi pack, so its config directory and the OS keychain are reachable. Everything else outside the worktree is not."],
    ["Does it change Pi anywhere else?", "No. The pi on PATH in an Ouijit terminal is a wrapper around the real one, and only there. Pi's own subcommands, such as install and config, pass straight through."],
  ]}
/>
